            <ArticleTitle>A case of multivessel coronary artery spasm resulting in wandering ST segment elevation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>121-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a case of recurrent episodes of resting myocardial ischaemia associated with ST elevation on ECG in different territories. Multivessel coronary artery spasm was demonstrated that was reversed with intracoronary glycerine trinitrate.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
